# SEQUENCE 14 - WHAT WAS DUE

EXT. OKU FAMILY HOUSE - FRONT VERANDA - EARLY AFTERNOON

The market bags arrive before anybody explains the faces carrying them.

Bode sets tomatoes and pepper on the veranda table.

Eno looks at the bags.

Then at Kai's hand.

The tremor is back.

Ade still has one thumb pressed below his ear.

Malik is breathing normally.

He does not trust that yet.

ENO
You found pepper.

BODE
Yes.

ENO
And?

Nobody answers.

Eno looks at Bode.

He tries to hold her gaze.

Cannot.

Kai does it for him.

KAI
It happened there.

ENO
At the market.

Kai nods.

Eno looks across the courtyard.

The compound gate.

The front room.

The kitchen.

The mouth of the back passage.

All ordinary in daylight.

ENO
Yesterday the house.

She looks back at them.

ENO
Today the market.

ADE
We're covering ground.

The joke lands nowhere.

Ade lets it die.

Eno remembers something.

ENO
You said something was late.

Malik looks at her.

MALIK
Nine days.

ENO
What was it?

MALIK
We don't know yet.

ENO
Then find that first.

BODE
Eno --

ENO
I did not say fix anything.

To Malik.

ENO
Find out what was late.

Malik looks toward the back passage.

Then to Kai.

Then Ade.

He does not decide for them.

MALIK
Room only.

KAI
Room only.

Ade nods.

ADE
Together.

Bode picks up the household keys.

CUT TO:

INT. OKU FAMILY HOUSE - BACK PASSAGE - MOMENTS LATER

Daylight reaches halfway down the passage.

The rest waits in cool shadow.

At the low end, Bode works the knot in the outer RED CORD open by hand.

The brothers stand behind him.

Nobody crowds the door.

Bode unlocks it.

The four stone steps descend into the maintenance room.

Kai's right hand twitches once at his side.

Malik sees it.

MALIK
If anything feels wrong, we leave.

KAI
If I say something feels wrong.

Malik starts to answer.

Ade gets there first.

ADE
Any one of us.

A beat.

Malik nods.

MALIK
Any one of us.

They go down together.

INT. OKU FAMILY HOUSE - MAINTENANCE ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Daylight through the high slats.

Camphor.

Paper.

Machine oil.

Nothing waits for them.

The INNER DOOR remains closed.

The field of red cord around it hangs still.

Malik stops.

Two knots sit below the pencil marks that once met them.

A loose tail rests at a different angle from the rows beside it.

He takes one step closer.

Stops before touching anything.

MALIK
Was that like that?

Kai looks only long enough to understand what Malik means.

KAI
No.

ADE
Nobody came down here last night.

BODE
No.

Malik studies the exposed pencil above the two lowered knots.

He reaches toward one.

Stops himself.

MALIK
Don't touch them.

Kai looks at him.

KAI
I wasn't.

Malik realizes who he was talking to.

MALIK
I know.

He backs away from the door.

That costs him something.

They move to the worktable.

Malik opens Solomon's ledger to the maintenance schedule.

The missed date waits where they left it.

Nine days late.

Kai stays on the far side of the table, his body angled away from the inner door.

Ade takes the chair that lets him see both brothers and the stone steps.

Bode remains beside the cabinet.

Malik turns to the index.

BINDING MATERIALS.
BRASS.
WESTERN STONES.
RIVER LEVEL.
INNER FRAME.

He begins matching entries.

One completed date.

Another.

Another.

Kai watches the pattern form before Malik says it.

Each scheduled interval has companion entries elsewhere in the ledger.

CHECKED.

MEASURED.

CLEAN.

A number changes --

then:

REPLACED.

RESET.

RE-MEASURED.

Malik goes back again.

Same order.

Different result.

KAI
He didn't know what he was going to repair.

Malik looks at the page.

MALIK
No.

He finds another interval.

The inspection comes first.

The correction comes after.

Malik looks at the missed date.

MALIK
This wasn't a repair date.

ADE
What was it?

MALIK
A check.

Kai moves closer to the table.

MALIK
He scheduled the inspection.

Malik turns one page.

MALIK
Then what he did depended on what moved.

Silence.

For the first time, the nine-day delay becomes something they can understand without understanding why it matters.

Kai looks at the index.

KAI
So we check.

MALIK
We measure.

KAI
Same thing.

MALIK
No.

Kai looks at him.

Malik catches the old reflex before it becomes a command.

MALIK
Not for you.

Kai absorbs that.

Not insulted.

Not reassured.

MALIK
If something changes when you look at it, you don't keep looking just because I need an answer.

KAI
Then what am I doing there?

Ade leans forward.

ADE
Telling us when the room stops being the room.

Kai looks at him.

ADE
You don't chase it.

To Malik.

ADE
You don't make him.

Malik holds Ade's gaze.

MALIK
Okay.

Kai looks back to the ledger.

KAI
And you?

ADE
I make sure both of you remember we can leave.

A beat.

Bode looks at the three brothers.

He hears the structure before they do.

He says nothing.

Malik turns pages again.

He writes on the back of the market receipt.

WESTERN STONES.

RIVER LEVEL.

INNER FRAME.

He stops before writing BRASS.

All four men look toward the ceiling -- toward the house above them, where the talisman remains under ordinary cloth.

Malik leaves BRASS off the list.

MALIK
We don't move it.

KAI
Agreed.

Malik looks toward the inner door.

MALIK
We don't adjust anything down here either.

ADE
Measure. Don't repair.

BODE
And the western stones?

Kai's jaw tightens.

The shrine lies below them somewhere beyond that part of the land.

MALIK
We stay on the path.

KAI
And if the path isn't where it was?

Nobody answers immediately.

Ade reaches over.

Taps the receipt once.

ADE
Then one of us says stop.

Malik nods.

Kai nods.

Bode does too.

At the top of the stone steps --

Eno.

She has not entered the room.

ENO
Well?

Malik turns toward her.

MALIK
The date was an inspection.

ENO
Can you do it?

Malik looks at Kai.

Kai looks at Ade.

Ade looks at Bode.

Only then does Malik answer.

MALIK
We can check what changed.

ENO
Today?

Malik hesitates.

That is answer enough.

ENO
No.

MALIK
Every day makes it later.

Eno looks at the dried blood still caught at the edge of Ade's nostril.

Kai's shaking hand.

Malik's too-careful breathing.

ENO
You already lost blood.

She steps back from the doorway.

ENO
Today you eat.

A beat.

ENO
Tomorrow you inspect.

Nobody argues.

Malik closes Solomon's ledger.

Kai leaves his aunt's notebook where it is.

Ade takes the market receipt with the three locations on it.

Bode turns toward the stairs.

They leave the room without touching the cord field.

Behind them --

The inner door remains closed.

Two knots remain below their pencil marks.

CUT TO BLACK.
